$image2image — image-to-image transform (prompt-guided)

SUMMARY
  Takes each link in images[] and produces a new image using the joined
  prompt text (instruction body and/or prompts[]). Replaces the images array
  with the new outputs.

SYNTAX
  $image2image
  $image2image(model='default')

INPUT
  images[] — source image(s) to transform.
  prompts[] / prompt_text — guidance text (newline-joined).

OUTPUT
  images[] — one new link per input image (replaces previous images list).

ARGUMENTS
  model= — reserved for future backend selection (current handler emulated).

BEHAVIOR
  Current implementation is emulated: writes placeholder PNGs that record
  the prompt and source link. If images[] is empty but prompt_text is set,
  emits one placeholder image from the prompt alone.

EXAMPLE
  @correct_image: $image2image
  correct hands

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  Yes — prompts cleared after call (runtime default for this name).
